## Based on https://jasonstitt.com/gitignore-whitelisting-patterns

# 1. Ignore everything
*

# 2. But descend into directories
!*/

# 3. Allow specific files and file extensions
!.gitignore
!LICENSE
!*.py
!*.sh
!*.md
!docs/*.html
!*.json
!uv.lock
!pyproject.toml


# 4. Block specific directories and files
.git/
**/.pytest_cache
**/.venv
docs/features/**/proof/runs

# Local security register
README.private.md

# Keep private conversations and local metadata out of public commits.
docs/interactions/

# Keep personal deliverables and runtime evidence outside public commits.
/docs/artifacts/
/docs/interactions/
/.private/
/private-data/
/privacy-backups/
/data/private/
/data/results/
